    <briefdescription>
<para>For simple types the main extension point for adding argument conversions is <ref refid="namespaceargagg_1_1convert_1acbfa15a31486143d3c2032b4ac78fa96" kindref="member">argagg::convert::arg&lt;T&gt;()</ref>. However, for complex types such as templated types partial specialization of a helper struct is required. This struct provides that extension point. The default, generic implementation of <ref refid="namespaceargagg_1_1convert_1acbfa15a31486143d3c2032b4ac78fa96" kindref="member">argagg::convert::arg&lt;T&gt;()</ref> calls <ref refid="structargagg_1_1convert_1_1converter_1a9ae0fc72243699c930acdb3a12fcb550" kindref="member">converter&lt;T&gt;::convert()</ref>. </para>
